  "scope": "Direct third-party dependencies of the implemented Go modules (every go/*/go.mod direct require -- no '// indirect' marker) and the npm packages under web/packages (package.json dependencies plus peerDependencies -- what a consumer installs because of a package; devDependencies are dev tooling, never shipped, and excluded). Workspace-internal modules (@speed/*, github.com/vislake/speed/go/*) are not external dependencies and carry no license entry. Policies applied here, mirroring docs/internal/20-quality-and-security.md: strong copyleft (GPL/AGPL) is banned; weak copyleft (MPL/LGPL) passes only with an ADR recording the adjudication (none exists today); anything not recognized fails with an adjudication message. Licenses were identified from the license file each release ships (see per-entry evidence); the license_scan.py --check run re-derives the expected dependency set from the tree and fails on any drift: a new or removed direct dependency, a version or used_by change, or an entry whose license violates policy."
